  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi recently participated in the 23rd ASEAN-India summit and the Quad meetings in Manila, where he addressed topics including Indo-Pacific security, digital cooperation, and regional stability. During these engagements, the Prime Minister advocated for cooperation over competition and proposed the introduction of e-visas for ASEAN tourists. Following his return, he convened a session with his Council of Ministers to address domestic governance. Key agenda items included the assessment of poverty reduction programs and the state's continued effort to eliminate left-wing extremism. Additionally, the Prime Minister emphasized the necessity of a sustained government campaign to combat the illegal drug trade and urged ministers to maintain financial prudence in public spending. These domestic focus areas follow a period of intense international diplomatic activity involving bilateral exchanges and collaborative security initiatives with partner nations.",
